# RU ↔ EN documentation mirrors

When creating or editing documentation under `docs-zensical/docs/ru/` or `docs-zensical/docs/en/`, always update the **mirror file** in the other language with the **same meaning and structure**.

## Mirror path

| Edited | Mirror |
|--------|--------|
| `docs-zensical/docs/ru/.../file.md` | `docs-zensical/docs/en/.../file.md` |
| `docs-zensical/docs/en/.../file.md` | `docs-zensical/docs/ru/.../file.md` |

Same relative path after `docs/ru/` ↔ `docs/en/`.

## Workflow

1. Edit (or create) the file in the language you are working in.
2. Resolve the mirror path (`ru` ↔ `en`).
3. Write the **same content** in the other language: same sections, tables, lists, diagrams, links (locale-adjusted), and frontmatter shape.
4. Do not leave one locale ahead of the other in the same change set.
5. If the mirror is missing — **create it**.
6. If a path has no locale pair by design (rare) — say so explicitly; do not silently skip.

## What must stay identical

- Section order and heading hierarchy
- Tables (rows/columns); translate cell text
- Mermaid diagrams (node labels may be translated; topology stays the same)
- Requirement IDs (`FR-О-01`, `UC-К-25`, `NFR-19`, `П-К-01`, `T_кулдаун`)
- Product UI strings stay in Russian in both locales (`«Принять»`, `«Я ищу работу»`). The KADRY interface is Russian (NFR-17).
- Links: point to the same doc in the **target** locale when a mirror exists

## What to translate

- Prose, headings, table labels, captions, list items
- Do not translate requirement IDs or quoted UI labels
